geCount":346,"summary":"How the breeding of new animals and plants was central to fascist regimes in Italy, Portugal, and Germany and to their imperial expansion. In the fascist regimes of Mussolini's Italy, Salazar's Portugal, and Hitler's Germany, the first mass mobilizations involved wheat engineered to take advantage of chemical fertilizers, potatoes resistant to late blight, and pigs that thrived on national produce. Food independence was an early goal of fascism; indeed, as Tiago Saraiva writes in Fascist Pigs, fascists were obsessed with projects to feed the national body from the national soil. Saraiva shows how such technoscientific organisms as specially bred wheat and pigs became important elements in the institutionalization and expansion of fascist regimes. The pigs, the potatoes, and the wheat embodied fascism.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-fascist-pigs-technoscientific-organisms-and-the-history-of-fascism-tiago-saraiva.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.074,"accessibilityScore":0.019,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"synthesis","score":0.2,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"from\"","catalog text contains \"history of\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":18,"criticalRenown":69,"controversy":19,"llmAffinity":78,"affinityResidual":6.32,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.78,"controversy":0.68,"llmAffinity":0.84},"tags":{"craft":"craft-of-explanation","evidence":"archival-research","stance":"conceptual-strangeness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Mussolini","confidence":0.98},{"name":"Salazar","confidence":0.98},{"name":"Hitler","confidence":0.98}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Italy","confidence":0.98},{"name":"Portugal","confidence":0.98},{"name":"Germany","confidence":0.98}],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The breeding of animals and plants hel